{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>to scratch himself</b> — to scrape. It has no parallel in Scripture. And some say: חֶרֶס [potsherd] is like: with a potsherd and with a sherd." "<b>among the ashes</b> — in the manner of mourning, 'and put on sackcloth and sit on ashes.' And the one who says that his sitting in ashes was to cool the sores needs to bring proof that the sores were hot and moist."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:32.974257812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}